  <prompt>
    Wire the `TRIAGE-EMAIL` Action (authored in 022) into the pipeline: author its Binding, its mirror-first input/output schema, a golden-utterance eval case, RAG grounding on the matter's correspondence, and the enrichment/event trigger — all reached via the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade (ADR-013). This is code-directed Action + Binding (ADR-039) — MUST NOT land on the frozen node-graph engine.

    1. **Binding row** — add a `sprk_playbookconsumer` Binding for `TRIAGE-EMAIL` to `infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json`, following the shape of the existing rows; seed it via `scripts/dataverse/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1`.
    2. **Mirror-first input schema** — author the input schema in `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/` (mirror-first per the consumer-wiring guide; use `create-task-v1.input.schema.json` as the reference shape). The input MUST feed the ALREADY-PRODUCED classification signal (`AiClassificationRung`/`CommunicationClassificationResult`) into the Action — NOT re-run a full classification pass (FR-05 efficiency rule from 022). Author the output schema for `{category, summary, obligations[], priority, reviewOutcome}`.
    3. **RAG grounding (FR-06)** — ground the classification/summary in the matter's OWN prior correspondence (already indexed). Wire the retrieval so triage improves with matter context vs a context-free pass; the eval case must DEMONSTRATE the improvement.
    4. **Golden-utterance eval case (NFR-07)** — add a golden-utterance eval case for the Action/Binding (blocking merge gate). It MUST demonstrate: the structured triage output on a representative inbound email AND the FR-06 context-improvement (matter-grounded vs context-free).
    5. **Enrichment/event trigger** — trigger the Action on the enrichment/event path via the `PublicContracts` facade (`ICommunicationClassificationAi` / the triage seam). The trigger MUST be **best-effort / non-fatal (NFR-04)** — a triage failure MUST NOT fail the capture or send path. Where the classification rung already ran, feed its result — no second full LLM pass.

    Validate with `jps-validate`. Run `scripts/Refresh-ScopeModelIndex.ps1` after authoring so the scope catalog reflects the new Action. This task does NOT persist the output to `sprk_communication` (that is task 025) — it produces the triage output and grounds/evaluates it.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke AI consumer-wiring engineer. Fluent in `ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md` (Action + Binding authoring, mirror-first input schemas, all entry paths, eval-case obligation), the `SPAARKE-PLAYBOOK-LLM-OUTPUT-PATTERN`, ADR-039 (closed catalog), ADR-013 (`PublicContracts` facade only — no AI internals in Communication code), NFR-04 (best-effort/non-fatal), NFR-07 (golden-utterance eval as a blocking gate), and the existing enrichment path. You wire via facades, ground in matter context, and never fail capture on a triage error.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `TRIAGE-EMAIL` is fully wired: a `sprk_playbookconsumer` Binding (seeded), a mirror-first input schema (feeding the produced classification signal — no second full pass) + output schema for the five fields, RAG grounding on the matter's correspondence, a golden-utterance eval case demonstrating the structured output AND the FR-06 context improvement, and an enrichment/event trigger via the `PublicContracts` facade that is best-effort/non-fatal (a triage failure never fails capture/send). `jps-validate` passes; the scope index is refreshed. Build clean; the eval-case gate passes; publish-size delta ≈0 (reuses the AI stack) + no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      022 authored the `TRIAGE-EMAIL` Action definition (reusing the classification signal). This task makes it live on the enrichment/event path: the Binding + input/output schema (ADR-039 closed catalog), RAG grounding in the matter's correspondence (FR-06 — classification improves with matter context), the NFR-07 eval case (blocking merge gate), and the trigger via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (ADR-013 — no AI internals in Communication code). The trigger is best-effort (NFR-04 / ADR-045 NFR-06): triage runs on the enrichment path but a failure MUST NOT fail capture or send. Where `AiClassificationRung` already produced a classification, the Action consumes it — no second full LLM pass (the FR-05 efficiency rule).

      Placement (§10): the wiring lands in shared `Services/Communication/` (the enrichment/event trigger) reaching AI ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (`ICommunicationClassificationAi` / the triage seam) — no `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` injected into Communication code (NFR-03/ADR-013). Triage adds no new heavy dependency (reuses the AI stack) → publish delta ≈0.
